{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>he shall take two male lambs without blemish and one ewe lamb</b>. Scripture did not specify what is to be done with the two male lambs and the ewe lamb, but it did mention concerning the one male lamb that he shall offer it as a guilt offering (Leviticus 14:12), and it mentioned that he shall perform the sin offering and afterward slaughter the burnt offering (Leviticus 14:19). This is because it had already stated in the section of Vayikra (Leviticus 5:5–6) concerning a sin offering that it is to be female, and it stated concerning every burnt offering (Leviticus 1:1–3 and elsewhere) that it is male; therefore there was no need to elaborate, for it is known that the second male lamb will be the burnt offering and the ewe lamb is the sin offering."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:53:46.795254715Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}